            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Demand Thresholds for  the pickup delay :</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Choose values between 0 and 1 (normalized pickup delay scale) to set thresholds for </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f9a655' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>moderate</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>, </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ee4115' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>high</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>, and </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff2600' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>very high</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> demand. The threshold for moderate demand should be the lowest, while the threshold for very high demand should be the highest.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Order Volume Threshold:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Set a value between 0 and 1, representing the order volume percentile. This threshold will help us filter out hexagons with a very low number of orders.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
